From e4b71bb0d36f500f55601eb13d04ae3bf1ca58c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:13:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] test(ui): the colour guard strips comments after code and
 joins theme_files

Review of #3990: the guard skipped only lines that start with `//`. A
comment inside a call hid a literal (`from_rgb(1, // red` counted 0),
and a colour in a comment after code counted 1. The scanner now
removes `//` and nested `/* */` comments and keeps the text of string
and char literals. Tests pin the two review probes, a `//` in a string
and in a raw string, a quote char literal, a lifetime, and a nested
block comment.

The guard moves into the theme_files suite (#3187: no new test binary).
Its scanner is split into theme_files/colour_scan.rs (400-line law).
The theme_files gate map names ui::egui_app, so each UI change runs it.

Refs #1120

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
